 :node    "naphtali"
 :requires #{:nbb :git}
 :test-cmd "kbb --backend sci --classpath src:test run-tests.cljs"
 :budget  {:max-turns 18 :max-tool-calls 45 :max-tokens 4000
           :deadline-ms 1200000 :test-timeout-ms 180000}
 :expect  {:files-subset-of ["src/delta/op.cljc" "test/delta/op_test.cljc"]
           :must-touch ["src/delta/op.cljc" "test/delta/op_test.cljc"]
           :max-files 2
           :must-add [":on-conflict" "deftest"]}
 :prompt
 "Task: extend an existing function without changing what current callers see.

  `delta.op/replay` stops at the first conflict and returns the conflict.

  1. Add an optional options argument so it can be called as
     (replay files ops) — unchanged behaviour — or
     (replay files ops {:on-conflict :skip}), where :skip skips the conflicting
     op, keeps going, and reports how many ops were skipped under a :skipped
     key in the returned map.
  2. Every existing test must still pass unchanged: the two-argument call must
     behave exactly as it does today, conflict shape included.
  3. Add a deftest in test/delta/op_test.cljc covering the :skip path.
  4. Run the whole test suite and make sure it is green.

  Touch only src/delta/op.cljc and test/delta/op_test.cljc."}
